WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.633
This is Stacks.

2
00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:04.920
It gives your AI agent a library card.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.467
Public libraries don't have an API.

4
00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:10.389
Whether a book is on the shelf, how long

5
00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:12.985
the hold queue is, when a branch closes:

6
00:00:12.985 --> 00:00:15.582
it all lives on websites built for people.

7
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.880
So AI assistants guess.

8
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.354
So let's ask a real question, live, in Claude

9
00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:20.690
Desktop.

10
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.361
I'm in Toronto.

11
00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:25.216
Is Project Hail Mary on the shelf anywhere

12
00:00:25.216 --> 00:00:25.930
right now?

13
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.222
Claude reaches for Stacks.

14
00:00:28.222 --> 00:00:30.219
It searches Toronto's catalogue, then checks

15
00:00:30.219 --> 00:00:32.549
every copy at every branch, live, through

16
00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:33.548
a TinyFish browser.

17
00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:36.211
Then it pulls today's hours for the branches

18
00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:37.210
that have it.

19
00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:39.112
And there's the answer.

20
00:00:39.112 --> 00:00:42.184
Two copies on the shelf right now, at Northern

21
00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:44.573
District and Barbara Frum, both open until

22
00:00:44.573 --> 00:00:45.256
eight thirty.

23
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:47.303
Real shelf data, read seconds ago.

24
00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:48.327
Not a guess.

25
00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:51.591
Under the hood, all five TinyFish engines

26
00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:52.668
do real work.

27
00:00:52.668 --> 00:00:55.182
Browser reads the pages, Fetch checks them,

28
00:00:55.182 --> 00:00:57.336
Search finds new libraries, Agent answers

29
00:00:57.336 --> 00:00:59.850
open questions, and Monitor watches a book

30
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.927
until it's back.

31
00:01:01.377 --> 00:01:03.874
And when a library's website changes, Stacks

32
00:01:03.874 --> 00:01:04.587
breaks loudly.

33
00:01:04.587 --> 00:01:06.370
This week the platform updated.

34
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.224
The daily canary caught it, an agent diagnosed

35
00:01:09.224 --> 00:01:12.077
it, and the fix shipped the next day.

36
00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:12.948
Stacks.

37
00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:15.055
Fourteen tools, fifty-four library systems,

38
00:01:15.055 --> 00:01:16.318
built with TinyFish.

39
00:01:16.318 --> 00:01:19.267
It's open source, so try it today.
